    <statement><p>Let <m>\mathbf{F} \left( x, y \right) = \frac{-y \mathbf{i} + x \mathbf{j}}{x^{2} +
y^{2}}</m> and let C be the circle <m>\mathbf{r} \left( t \right) = \left( \cos t
\right) \mathbf{i} + \left( \sin t \right) \mathbf{j}</m>, <m>0 \leq t \leq 2\pi</m>.</p>
<p>A. Compute <m>\frac{\partial Q}{\partial x}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
<p>Note: Your answer should be an expression of x and y; e.g. "3xy - y"</p>
<p>B. Compute <m>\frac{\partial P}{\partial y}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
<p>Note: Your answer should be an expression of x and y; e.g. "3xy - y"</p>
<p>C. Compute <m>\int_C \mathbf{F} \cdot d\mathbf{r}</m></p>
<p><fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
<p>Note: Your answer should be a number</p>
<p>D. Is <alert> F </alert> conservative? Type Y if yes, type N if no.</p>
<p><fillin characters="40" name="AnSwEr0004"/></p>
</statement>
